@startuml
title SplitSmart pairwise payment settlement
actor "Authorized payer" as Payer
participant "Client" as Client
participant "RecordPayment use case" as App
participant "Pair and policy validation" as Domain
database "Transaction / repositories" as Store
queue "Notification outbox" as Outbox

Payer -> Client : record payment to named payee
Client -> App : record(group, payer, payee, amount, date, requestId)
App -> Domain : authorize; validate positive exact amount,\ndistinct endpoints and same group/currency pair
alt invalid pair, unauthorized, or invalid amount
  Domain --> App : explicit validation error
  App --> Client : reject; no financial facts
else valid request
  App -> Store : begin transaction; check idempotency and current pair balance
  alt duplicate request
    Store --> App : prior result
    App --> Client : return same committed result; no second posting
  else stale version / wrong pair / policy violation
    Store --> App : conflict or explicit rejection
    App --> Client : reject; no changes
  else overpayment policy unresolved or exceeded
    Store --> App : rollback
    App --> Client : explicit policy error; no posted payment
  else valid settlement
    App -> Store : insert committed PostedPayment
    App -> Store : insert exactly one LedgerEntry with unique payment source key
    App -> Store : update or mark only named pair projection dirty
    App -> Outbox : enqueue notices in same transaction
    alt transaction failure
      Store --> App : rollback payment and posting
      App --> Client : explicit failure
    else commit
      Store --> App : payment + one posting + pair result
      App --> Client : settlement recorded and balance updated
    end
  end
end
note over Store
Payment and its one ledger posting commit atomically. A pending/failed
PaymentAttempt is not a posted financial fact and has no ledger entry.
Overpayment, semantic duplicate and reversal policies require owner approval.
end note
@enduml
